            <ArticleTitle>Clinical management of cardiogenic shock associated with prolonged propofol infusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>221-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report details the development of cardiogenic shock after craniotomy in a patient sedated with a propofol infusion. The patient survived with the assistance of extracorporeal membrane oxygenation. A literature review summarizes the syndrome of cardiogenic shock associated with prolonged propofol infusion. This is the first report of survival in this syndrome resuiting from mechanical circulatory support.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
